, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-1,2]$ since it is continuous over $x\\in [-1,2]$ except at the point $x=1,$ where the one-sided limits exist and are finite:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)=6\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)$ is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-1,2]$ since it is continuous over $x\\in [-1,2].$\n\n- The function $h(x)$ is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-1,2]$ since it is continuous over $x\\in [-1,2].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$f,g,$ and $h.$\"" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317814 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317815 13194139534891 true] [17592186317814 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317816 13194139534891 true] [17592186317814 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317817 13194139534891 true] [17592186317814 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317818 13194139534891 true] [17592186317814 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317819 13194139534891 true] [17592186317814 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534891 true] [17592186317814 1041 "selection" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317814 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317816 13194139534891 true] [17592186317814 1110 #uuid "38946df1-1937-57d3-8ebb-2d5ae7a6e14c" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317815 1034 "$f$ and $g$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317815 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317815 1111 #uuid "3922de2b-4290-5f29-a23b-44977f73451f" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317816 1034 "$f,g,$ and $h$" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317816 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317816 1111 #uuid "25269ca1-4940-5a95-ad2b-837c29b40599" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317817 1034 "$g$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317817 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317817 1111 #uuid "1bd5c92b-6d7d-5e2a-8ddc-c5c6d8797ffe" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317818 1034 "$f$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317818 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317818 1111 #uuid "4fd0fac0-14c8-5fe7-adef-fc06b1