ous over $x\\in [0,2]$ since it is continuous over $x\\in [0,2].$\n\n- The function $h(x)$ is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2]$ since it is continuous over $x\\in [0,2]$ except at the point $x=1,$ where the one-sided limits exist and are finite:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}h(x)=3,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}h(x)=2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$g$ and $h$ only.\"" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317836 13194139534891 true] [17592186317835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317837 13194139534891 true] [17592186317835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317838 13194139534891 true] [17592186317835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317839 13194139534891 true] [17592186317835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317840 13194139534891 true] [17592186317835 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534891 true] [17592186317835 1041 "selection" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317835 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317838 13194139534891 true] [17592186317835 1110 #uuid "2cdcf774-d30a-552b-9bfd-cf8b6fe0b5b4" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317836 1034 "$f,g,$ and $h$" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317836 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317836 1111 #uuid "d0521f22-b354-56a2-a59c-1cd9a2088a73" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317837 1034 "$g$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317837 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317837 1111 #uuid "433f8338-e09a-588d-845b-33eb4b487d15" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317838 1034 "$g$ and $h$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317838 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317838 1111 #uuid "d9eb153e-c748-5eae-a6e4-64964b5d01a0" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317839 1034 "$f$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317839 1111 #uuid "cc85fd89-6175-5ae6-9cdd-386e45657504" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317840 1034 "$f$ and $h$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317840 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317840 1111 #uuid "c3