 .\n$$\n\n- The function $h(x)$ is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,\\infty )$ since it is continuous over $x\\in [0,\\infty )$ except at the points $x=2$ and $x=5,$ where the one-sided limits exist and are finite:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}h(x)=0,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}h(x)=1\n$$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}h(x)=1,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{+}}h(x)=2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$h$ only.\"" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317871 13194139534891 true] [17592186317870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317872 13194139534891 true] [17592186317870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317873 13194139534891 true] [17592186317870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317874 13194139534891 true] [17592186317870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317875 13194139534891 true] [17592186317870 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534891 true] [17592186317870 1041 "selection" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317870 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317871 13194139534891 true] [17592186317870 1110 #uuid "685c626e-eee7-531b-bef7-6c143fe01f36" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317871 1034 "$h$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317871 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317871 1111 #uuid "0218821f-31d1-5b08-961d-1565e1257e6b" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317872 1034 "$g$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317872 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317872 1111 #uuid "04369ebd-82bb-5139-b0e4-fa0ae64ff8e0" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317873 1034 "$g$ and $h$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317873 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317873 1111 #uuid "8e9f4149-9bc7-5fc8-a259-1b51d502b13d" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317874 1034 "$f$ and $h$" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317874 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317874 1111 #uuid "30c7f37d-585d-5706-af93-b2f11c51ee0e" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317875 1034 "$f$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317875 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317875 1111 #uuid "bf690455-290a-51fa-99f6-095fab8bc757" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317876 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317877 13194139534891 true] [17592186317876 1089 "q-394127" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317876 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534891 true] [17592186317876 1100 "Which of the following functions are piecewise smooth on $x\\in [-1,1]?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=2x+\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{2}},\\,g(x)={\\begin{aligned}-4x+1, & x<0 \\\\ -4x+3, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\\,,\\,h(x)=x\\sqrt[5]{x}\n$$" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317876 1113 #uuid "db6f9fc1-3b02-5615-8e6c-477c7f6565ff" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317876 1145 "A function $f(x)$ is **piecewise smooth** on $x\\in [a,b]$ if\n\n- $f(x)$ is piecewise continuous on $[a,b],$ and\n\n- ${f}^{′}(x)$ exists and is continuous except possibly at finitely many points, where its one-sided limits exist and are finite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $f(x)=2x+\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{2}}$ is not piecewise smooth on $x\\in [-1,1].$ We split the interval at $x=0$ into the two open intervals $(-1,0)$ and $(0,1).$ For $x\\ne 0,$\n\n$$\nf(x)=2x+{x}^{2/5},\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=2+\\frac{2}{5{x}^{3/5}}.\n$$\n\nWhile this derivative is continuous on the open pieces $(-1,0)$ and $(0,1),$ the limits of the derivative as $x\\to 0$ are not finite. In fact, the derivative becomes unbounded near $x=0.$ Thus, the condition for finite limits at the endpoints is not met.\n\n- The function $g(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in [-1,1].$ We split the interval at $x=0.$ On each open interval, $(-1,0)$ and $(0,1),$ the function is linear. On these intervals,\n\n$$\ng(x)={\\begin{aligned}-4x+1, & x<0 \\\\ -4x+3, & x>0\\end{aligned}\\,,\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)={\\begin{aligned}-4, & x<0 \\\\ -4, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $g(x)$ and ${g}^{′}(x)$ are piecewise continuous on each open interval, and they both have finite limits at the endpoints of the subintervals.\n\n- The function $h(x)=x\\sqrt[5]{x}$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in [-1,1].$ Since\n\n$$\nh(x)={x}^{6/5},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)=\\frac{6}{5}{x}^{1/5}.\n$$\n\nHere, $h(x)$ and ${h}^{′}(x)$ are continuous on $[-1,1].$ Thus, $h(x)$ is continuously differentiable on the whole interval, and hence piecewise smooth.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$g$ and $h$ only.\"" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317878 13194139534891 true] [17592186317877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317879 13194139534891 true] [17592186317877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317880 13194139534891 true] [17592186317877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317881 13194139534891 true] [17592186317877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317882 13194139534891 true] [17592186317877 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534891 true] [17592186317877 1041 "selection" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317877 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317881 13194139534891 true] [17592186317877 1110 #uuid "be1e5df4-878e-5cf6-91eb-3f1054428f49" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317878 1034 "$f$ and $g$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317878 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317878 1111 #uuid "c82e9da9-cf38-5f44-8052-4d878745ee6f" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317879 1034 "$h$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317879 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317879 1111 #uuid "a3e5a6ec-5207-5e2e-881e-150f1ca16204" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317880 1034 "$g$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317880 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317880 1111 #uuid "a12733e2-84fd-5c52-b7fe-fdeed5d1c3b0" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317881 1034 "$g$ and $h$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317881 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317881 1111 #uuid "f48f6d2c-d34f-58b3-abd3-ce1342cab207" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317882 1034 "$f,$ $g,$ and $h$" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317882 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317882 1111 #uuid "42945a4b-b06a-5086-9770-851ba8bf2193" 131941395