\n\n$$\nh(x)={x}^{1/4},\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{4{x}^{3/4}}.\n$$\n\nWhile this derivative is continuous on the open piece $(0,1),$ the limit of the derivative as $x\\to {0}^{+}$ is not finite. In fact, the derivative becomes unbounded near $x=0.$ Thus, the condition for finite limits at the endpoints is not met.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$f$ only.\"" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317885 13194139534891 true] [17592186317884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317886 13194139534891 true] [17592186317884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317887 13194139534891 true] [17592186317884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317888 13194139534891 true] [17592186317884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317889 13194139534891 true] [17592186317884 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534891 true] [17592186317884 1041 "selection" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317884 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317889 13194139534891 true] [17592186317884 1110 #uuid "b1d1ae7b-abfe-5f90-98ac-d77131e11a10" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317885 1034 "$f$ and $g$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317885 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317885 1111 #uuid "bc981bd2-3ac7-5462-a2ba-ecd736bdbbc3" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317886 1034 "$g$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317886 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317886 1111 #uuid "c7e23482-d62f-59b3-b547-a3c1ed796551" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317887 1034 "$g$ and $h$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317887 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317887 1111 #uuid "58f5b303-9f8f-5ac6-917e-062734c7d83b" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317888 1034 "$f,$ $g,$ and $h$" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317888 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317888 1111 #uuid "e452dd22-2362-5a98-b894-2cc8597e9633" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317889 1034 "$f$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317889 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317889 1111 #uuid "b