-1,0)$ and $(0,1).$ For $x\\ne 0,$\n\n$$\ng(x)=4x-{x}^{3/7},\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)=4-\\frac{3}{7{x}^{4/7}}.\n$$\n\nWhile this derivative is continuous on the open pieces $(-1,0)$ and $(0,1),$ the limits of the derivative as $x\\to 0$ are not finite. In fact, the derivative becomes unbounded near $x=0.$ Thus, the condition for finite limits at the endpoints is not met.\n\n- The function $h(x)=3{x}^{2}+\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}}$ is not piecewise smooth on $x\\in [-1,1].$ We split the interval at $x=0$ into the two open intervals $(-1,0)$ and $(0,1).$ For $x\\ne 0,$\n\n$$\nh(x)=3{x}^{2}+{x}^{3/5},\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)=6x+\\frac{3}{5{x}^{2/5}}.\n$$\n\nWhile this derivative is continuous on the open pieces $(-1,0)$ and $(0,1),$ the limits of the derivative as $x\\to 0$ are not finite. In fact, the derivative becomes unbounded near $x=0.$ Thus, the condition for finite limits at the endpoints is not met.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the functions.\"" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317906 13194139534891 true] [17592186317905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317907 13194139534891 true] [17592186317905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317908 13194139534891 true] [17592186317905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317909 13194139534891 true] [17592186317905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317910 13194139534891 true] [17592186317905 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534891 true] [17592186317905 1041 "selection" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317905 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317908 13194139534891 true] [17592186317905 1110 #uuid "aad52def-c29b-5e93-924a-0e86a99ada14" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317906 1034 "$g$ only" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317906 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317906 1111 #uuid "805ac4f2-938b-50bd-b5ef-8668ea170e44" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317907 1034 "$f,$ $g,$ and $h$" 13194139534891 true] [17592186317907 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534891 true] [17592186317907 1111 #uuid "d6225cfb-3351-53f1-b33e-e2221fe6